    model3DPath: "", model3DScale: 0, model3DRotation: [0, 0, 0], manualLightPositions: {}, riskRating: 5, lightSettings: {}, hotspotSettings: {}, model3DHotspots: [], customLightNames: {}, author: "",
    drivingExperience: "The 367hp DLZA 3.0 TFSI in the all-new GU SQ5 is an absolute masterpiece of forced induction and hybridization. The integration of the 48V MHEV Plus system with a transmission-mounted Powertrain Generator entirely eliminates turbo lag, providing a violent, instantaneous surge of 550 Nm of torque from just above idle. It possesses an incredibly smooth, linear powerband that rewards revving it out. The heavy-duty 7-speed S-tronic automatic replaces the old ZF8, offering lightning-fast shifts in dynamic mode while retaining buttery smooth luxury cruising. The V6 exhaust note is throaty and aggressive, completing an incredibly engaging driving experience.",
    mechanicVerdict: "The 3.0 TFSI (DLZA) EA839 on the new PPC platform is an incredibly powerful and tunable engine. The catastrophic rocker arm failures of the 2017-2018 models are long gone; this engine core is virtually bulletproof. However, it introduces significant complexity. The 48V MHEV Plus system integrates the electric motor into the DL382+ transmission, meaning transmission fluid maintenance is absolutely non-negotiable. Furthermore, managing the intense heat of the Hot-V layout (which bakes the PCV and water pump over time) is your main priority. If maintained strictly, the DLZA will easily outlast the car. It is an exceptional performance SUV.",
    repairCostEstimate: "$1,200 - $2,500 / year (Routine maintenance is moderate, but the complex 48V system and DL382+ transmission require strict adherence to fluid change intervals. The primary expenses will be the inevitable water pump/thermostat replacement and PCV failure due to the extreme heat in the engine valley)"
